{"id": "lg_elec-2026-10-12-008", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec", "lg_display"], "customers": ["lg_elec"], "suppliers": ["lg_display"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["slow"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "China slows down, Korea invests again: is the OLED industry's balance of power shifting?", "content": "<p>For more than a decade, the story of the display industry has moved in one direction: China built, and Korea held. Chinese panel makers first overtook Korea in LCD, then spent heavily on 6-Gen flexible AMOLED lines, mostly financed by local governments and state-owned banks. China's share of global OLED capacity grew from only around 5% back in 2017 to over 40% in 2025 (this includes LG Display's Guangzhou fab). As recently as 2024, DSCC expected China to account for 85% of all display equipm", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/china-slows-down-korea-invests-again-oled-industrys-balance-power-shifting", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-009", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Microsoft's Maia 300 rack: 96 accelerators, HBM4, mostly liquid-cooled", "content": "Microsoft has released architecture details for Maia 300, its third-generation Azure AI accelerator. The design pairs 96 accelerators per rack with a two-tier network that links up to 12,288 accelerators into a single superpod. The company says the system is built for cloud-scale agentic inference, and that it co-designed the software, silicon, rack infrastructure, networking, and data centers to run as one platform.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261012VL207/microsoft-server-rack-hbm4-accelerator-switch.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-010", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "<sub></sub>Apple iPhone launch and holiday demand lift Momo revenue to a record September", "content": "Fubon Multimedia, which operates the Momo e-commerce platform, reported consolidated revenue of approximately NT$8.59 billion (US$269.4 million) in September 2026, up 8.2% from a year earlier. Revenue for the first nine months reached nearly NT$80 billion, an increase of about 3.9%, setting records for the period on both a monthly and cumulative basis.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261012PD246/fubon-demand-revenue-launch-iphone.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-011", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "HHGalaxy reports record 3Q26 revenue as Double 11 demand builds", "content": "Taiwanese e-commerce operations provider HHGalaxy reported consolidated revenue of NT$621 million (US$19.5 million) for September 2026, up 31.74% from a year earlier, as brands prepared for the Single's Day shopping event. Revenue for the first nine months reached NT$4.925 billion, a 26.76% annual increase, while third-quarter revenue rose 34.43% to NT$1.774 billion, setting a third-quarter record.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261012PD247/revenue-demand-e-commerce-data-taiwan.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-10-12-012", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung reportedly secures long-term contracts covering up to 80% of 2027 memory supply", "content": "Samsung Electronics has committed 75&ndash;80% of its 2027 memory supply, including high-bandwidth memory (HBM), to long-term agreements (LTAs), the <em>Korea Economic Daily</em> reported on October 9, 2026, citing industry sources. Nvidia, Google and Microsoft were among the major customers that had largely finalized contracts. Samsung has not confirmed the allocation or named the buyers.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261012VL226/samsung-2027-2026-hbm-data-center.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-013", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["[否定]record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "Nanya gross margin hits 85.7% as low-priced DRAM contracts roll off", "content": "Nanya Technology reported record quarterly earnings in the third quarter of 2026, according to unaudited results released on October 12, as DRAM average selling prices (ASPs) rose more than 60% sequentially following the expiration of low-priced long-term agreements (LTAs).", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261012PD236/nanya-technology-low-priced-dram-gross-margin-2026.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-014", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["[否定]record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "How 'Filter Moore's Law' is doubling revenue for a Taiwan chip filter maker", "content": "Under what the industry terms the \"Filter Moore's Law,\" each process node shrink lowers tolerance for airborne molecular contaminants, causing filtration demand to grow exponentially. For global airborne molecular contamination (AMC) filtration leader Ye Siang Enterprise, that demand is now showing up in record revenue.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261012PD221/revenue-2nm-expansion-packaging-2026.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-015", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Chenbro Micom expands into Nvidia Vera Rubin rack-scale systems, 2026 revenue already tops full-year 2025", "content": "Taiwanese server chassis maker Chenbro Micom is expanding its role in AI infrastructure, moving beyond traditional server enclosures into high-end AI servers and rack-level solutions. The company has secured involvement in multiple Nvidia Vera Rubin platform projects covering GPUs, CPUs, and storage, while custom ASIC programs for cloud service providers (CSPs) are gradually scaling up according to schedule.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261012VL223/chenbro-2026-chassis-revenue-nvidia.html", "type": "rss"}]}
